# Sourced by both ffmpeg builds — the Dockerfile's ffmpeg-builder stage and
# scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh for the desktop app. One place, so the container
# and the desktop app can't end up on ffmpeg versions that behave
# differently (see build/ffmpeg/README.md).
#
# **Track ffmpeg's current release branch.** This binary is a decoder fed
# untrusted input — a radio station's bytes go straight into its demuxers
# (core/radio_relay.py) — so sitting on a branch that has stopped getting
# point releases is a decision, not a default. That is how this got stuck
# once already: 8.1.2 was pinned in June 2026 because it was current, 9.0
# landed six weeks later, no 8.1.3 ever followed, and the app meanwhile
# documented measurements taken against 9.0.1 (the version a development
# checkout picks up off PATH) while shipping 8.1.2 to everyone else.
#
# Checking a bump is cheap and does not need hardware: build it and let
# scripts/check-ffmpeg-recipe.sh and scripts/verify-ffmpeg.sh answer. For
# 9.0.1 they did, with component lists byte-identical to 8.1.2's.
FFMPEG_VERSION=9.0.1
# Current as of 2026-09-08.
OPUS_VERSION=1.6.1
